# An unclosed `(` does not swallow the query on the next line (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
T | where f(a
U | take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..25
  PIPELINE@0..13
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "T"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..13
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      CALL_EXPR@10..13
        NAME_REF@10..11
          IDENT@10..11 "f"
        ARG_LIST@11..13
          L_PAREN@11..12 "("
          NAME_REF@12..13
            IDENT@12..13 "a"
  WHITESPACE@13..14 "\n"
  PIPELINE@14..24
    NAME_REF@14..15
      IDENT@14..15 "U"
    WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
    PIPE@16..17 "|"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    TAKE_OP@18..24
      IDENT@18..22 "take"
      WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
      LITERAL@23..24
        LONG@23..24 "1"
  WHITESPACE@24..25 "\n"

error[DS0112]: unclosed `(`
  --> query:1:12
  |
1 | T | where f(a
  |            ^ this `(` is never closed
2 | U | take 1
  | - expected `)` before this
  |
  = help: add `)` where the bracketed part ends
